{#- Once-per-suite mock-request-count helper (alef issue #433).

   Context variables (see src/e2e/codegen/mock_assertions/helper.rs for the full contract):
   - helper_name: function name
   - total_path: mock server's total-count endpoint path
   - one_path: mock server's single-key endpoint path

   Emits ONE sync function using only the standard library (urllib.request), so it adds no new
   dependency to the generated pyproject.toml. Callers build `path_and_query` from
   "{{ total_path }}?prefix=<p>" (mock.requests.total) or "{{ one_path }}?key=<k>"
   (mock.requests["<k>"]) -- see mock_assertions::model::MockQuery. An async test calls this via
   `asyncio.to_thread({{ helper_name }}, ...)` rather than calling it directly on the event loop.
#}
def {{ helper_name }}(base_url: str, path_and_query: str) -> int:
    import urllib.request

    with urllib.request.urlopen(f"{base_url}{path_and_query}") as response:
        body = response.read().decode("utf-8").strip()
    return int(body)
